VALUES (4400093531020112, ARRAY['"A site loads HTML and images, but not CSS; the CSS URL returns 404. What should be done first?"'::jsonb, '"A form needs one department choice and multiple interests; submitted values should be meaningful. Which combined setup is best?"'::jsonb, '"A page must fit a card within a 300 px border-box width including 20 px padding on each side and 2 px borders. With `box-sizing: border-box`, what content width remains?"'::jsonb, '"An external stylesheet sets a heading teal, but a normal class rule changes it to purple and an ID rule changes it to navy. With equal origin/importance, which usually wins?"'::jsonb, '"A page uses HTTPS but loads a third-party image with an HTTP URL. What is the best correction?"'::jsonb, '"A web server accepts requests by IP but a public domain fails after a deployment. The server logs show no request for the domain. Which path is most worth checking first?"'::jsonb, '"A developer creates a horizontal navigation bar and wants it to wrap on small screens while retaining a clear layout. Which approach is most suitable?"'::jsonb, '"An element must animate into view, but should not create a large movement for users who opt out of animation. What is the complete solution?"'::jsonb, '"A site has duplicate IDs because the same `id=\"menu\"` is applied to every navigation item. What change is appropriate if they share the same styling?"'::jsonb, '"A developer must deliver a linked external CSS file and a semantic HTML page. Which verification set is most complete?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Replace all images with tables"'::jsonb, '"Correct the link/path or restore the stylesheet at the requested URL, then retest the page"'::jsonb, '"Rewrite every CSS rule without checking the URL"'::jsonb, '"Change the HTML title"'::jsonb, '"Use unnamed radio inputs for everything"'::jsonb, '"Use a single hidden field and no visible controls"'::jsonb, '"Use a named radio group for department, named checkboxes for interests and a submit control"'::jsonb, '"Use table cells without a form"'::jsonb, '"276 px"'::jsonb, '"300 px"'::jsonb, '"260 px"'::jsonb, '"256 px"'::jsonb, '"The ID rule, because it has higher specificity"'::jsonb, '"The browser picks the first colour alphabetically"'::jsonb, '"The type selector, because it is external"'::jsonb, '"The class rule always beats an ID"'::jsonb, '"Change img to h1"'::jsonb, '"Switch DNS from IPv4 to CSS"'::jsonb, '"Use an HTTPS image endpoint or another secure resource source"'::jsonb, '"Put the image URL in a hidden input"'::jsonb, '"DNS records/propagation and client resolver cache"'::jsonb, '"CSS animation keyframes"'::jsonb, '"Form reset type"'::jsonb, '"HTML table spans"'::jsonb, '"Use a meta title to space items"'::jsonb, '"Use flexible layout rules such as flexbox with wrapping and appropriate spacing"'::jsonb, '"Position every item at a fixed viewport coordinate"'::jsonb, '"Make every link a background image"'::jsonb, '"Use only FTP"'::jsonb, '"Place animation instructions in alt text"'::jsonb, '"Use absolute positioning without considering user preference"'::jsonb, '"Use CSS animation/transform for the normal case and a reduced-motion media query to simplify or disable it"'::jsonb, '"Use a class for the repeated items and reserve IDs for unique elements"'::jsonb, '"Replace each ID with href"'::jsonb, '"Use colspan for each link"'::jsonb, '"Keep all duplicate IDs because they improve specificity"'::jsonb, '"Confirm only the domain name and stop"'::jsonb, '"Check only the page title"'::jsonb, '"Confirm stylesheet link/path, inspect loaded styles, validate element nesting and test links/image alt text at target sizes"'::jsonb, '"Verify only animation speed"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

