VALUES (440099110101019, ARRAY['"A project combines evidence about a historic water system with a modern proposal. Which conclusion is best supported by the syllabus without overclaiming?"'::jsonb, '"A student classifies six study notes: pronunciation, ritual method, grammar, word etymology, metre and calendar calculation. Which mapping places every note correctly?"'::jsonb, '"A presentation uses a mathematical example from an ancient text and says that it proves all current mathematics directly originated there. What is the key reasoning flaw?"'::jsonb, '"A student needs one theme that links Sanskrit language sciences with modern computation while staying within the syllabus. Which is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"A research poster covers iron/steel, textiles/dyeing, irrigation and transportation. Which structure best maintains analytical clarity?"'::jsonb, '"A student is asked to connect ecological practice, agriculture and settlement design. Which topics provide the clearest syllabus path?"'::jsonb, '"A case says a person prioritizes ethical duty, livelihood, enjoyment and liberation. Which framework is being applied?"'::jsonb, '"A student argues that Brahmacharya follows Vanaprastha because both involve withdrawal. What is the correct correction?"'::jsonb, '"A lesson compares Puranas, Itihasa and the Vedic corpus. Which categorization is most consistent with the syllabus?"'::jsonb, '"A researcher wants to claim a specific metal technology was used at a named site, but the course outline only lists metalworking generally. What should they do?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Water systems are covered only as philosophical symbols"'::jsonb, '"All historical systems are automatically more efficient than modern systems"'::jsonb, '"Every region used an identical water design"'::jsonb, '"The syllabus provides a basis to compare water-management approaches; effectiveness of a specific design still requires case evidence"'::jsonb, '"Shiksha, Kalpa, Vyakarana, Nirukta, Chandas, Jyotisha"'::jsonb, '"Kalpa, Chandas, Nirukta, Jyotisha, Shiksha, Vyakarana"'::jsonb, '"Vyakarana, Shiksha, Jyotisha, Chandas, Kalpa, Nirukta"'::jsonb, '"Nirukta, Jyotisha, Chandas, Vyakarana, Kalpa, Shiksha"'::jsonb, '"It cites the number system"'::jsonb, '"It extrapolates from one example to a universal historical claim without sufficient evidence"'::jsonb, '"It distinguishes source and interpretation"'::jsonb, '"It defines geometry too precisely"'::jsonb, '"Discuss only the mechanical keyboard"'::jsonb, '"Claim that all software must be written in Sanskrit"'::jsonb, '"Explain the stated relationship between Sanskrit and natural language processing"'::jsonb, '"Replace language analysis with a calendar chart"'::jsonb, '"Organize them as separate technology themes and compare each practice using relevant evidence and constraints"'::jsonb, '"Treat them as one identical process"'::jsonb, '"Put all evidence under the four Vedas"'::jsonb, '"Classify every theme as an Ashrama"'::jsonb, '"Only algebraic identities"'::jsonb, '"Only word-processing margins"'::jsonb, '"Nakshatrara Gyaan and agriculture; forest management and urban planning"'::jsonb, '"Only Vedic pronunciation and metre"'::jsonb, '"Forms of HTML"'::jsonb, '"Vedangas"'::jsonb, '"Computer ports"'::jsonb, '"Purusharthas"'::jsonb, '"Brahmacharya is a Veda"'::jsonb, '"Brahmacharya is the student stage and conventionally comes first; Vanaprastha follows Grihastha"'::jsonb, '"Vanaprastha is the goal of liberation"'::jsonb, '"The two terms refer to identical measurement units"'::jsonb, '"Puranas are CSS properties"'::jsonb, '"Itihasa is a unit of distance"'::jsonb, '"The Vedas form a core corpus; Puranas are described as encyclopaedic; Itihasa is a source of wisdom"'::jsonb, '"All three are names of Vedangas"'::jsonb, '"Find source evidence specific to that site before making the claim"'::jsonb, '"Replace evidence with a philosophical term"'::jsonb, '"Assume the outline proves it for every site"'::jsonb, '"Use the title of the unit as the sole evidence"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

