VALUES (4400991101010110, ARRAY['"A calendar dataset contains dates for ritual observances, but no source explains its calculation rules. What is the most defensible research step?"'::jsonb, '"A team has to explain Caturdaśa-Vidyāsthāna and avoid confusing it with Catur-Ashrama. Which distinction is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A text combines language analysis with calendar computation. Which two syllabus areas should be explicitly distinguished in its report?"'::jsonb, '"A comparison of two traditional water systems finds one suited to seasonal rainfall and another to a different local environment. Which conclusion is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"A student groups ethics, livelihood, enjoyment and liberation into four ''tools of architecture''. What is the precise correction?"'::jsonb, '"Which plan best evaluates a claim that ancient textile dyeing was a technical speciality?"'::jsonb, '"A project claims a town plan followed Vastu Shastra because it has a grid layout. Which added evidence would most strengthen the claim?"'::jsonb, '"A student must compare an epic narrative with a modern engineering record. Which approach matches the course framing of Itihasa as a source of wisdom?"'::jsonb, '"Which research claim most clearly stays within the outline when discussing ancient Indian mathematics?"'::jsonb, '"A study links sacred ecology with forest management and urban planning. Which combination is the most syllabus-aligned?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Use the calendar/timekeeping syllabus theme, then verify the dataset''s source and calculation method before interpreting it"'::jsonb, '"Assume each date was calculated identically across all historical periods"'::jsonb, '"Discard the source and invent a rule"'::jsonb, '"Classify the dataset as temple architecture"'::jsonb, '"Caturdaśa refers only to four Vedas"'::jsonb, '"Caturdaśa-Vidyāsthāna is a 14-part knowledge classification; the four Ashramas are life stages"'::jsonb, '"Ashramas are six Vedangas"'::jsonb, '"Both mean the four goals of life"'::jsonb, '"Itihasa and spreadsheet formulas"'::jsonb, '"Vastu and textile dyeing only"'::jsonb, '"Language sciences/Sanskrit and astronomy/Vedanga Jyotish"'::jsonb, '"Purusharthas and hardware ports"'::jsonb, '"One system must be superior everywhere"'::jsonb, '"The syllabus gives no permission to discuss water systems"'::jsonb, '"Only their names matter"'::jsonb, '"Design suitability depends on local conditions; compare storage, supply and maintenance evidence"'::jsonb, '"They are the four Vedas"'::jsonb, '"They are the Purusharthas, or goals of human life, not architecture tools"'::jsonb, '"They are measurement units"'::jsonb, '"They are six Vedangas"'::jsonb, '"Infer all details from the word ''speciality''"'::jsonb, '"Assume all fabrics used one dyeing method"'::jsonb, '"Use a calendar to prove the dye chemistry"'::jsonb, '"Describe the specific textile/dyeing process using credible evidence and distinguish it from a general course-level theme"'::jsonb, '"Source-specific historical documentation linking the plan to the relevant planning principles"'::jsonb, '"An unrelated HTML layout"'::jsonb, '"A list of the four Vedas only"'::jsonb, '"A statement that all grids are Vastu-based"'::jsonb, '"Assume an epic is a computer manual"'::jsonb, '"Ignore context and use it as a measurement standard"'::jsonb, '"Discuss the narrative''s cultural/ethical lessons separately from empirical engineering evidence"'::jsonb, '"Treat every narrative detail as a modern engineering specification"'::jsonb, '"A specific date is certain even though no evidence is supplied"'::jsonb, '"Every formula used today was invented in one ancient text"'::jsonb, '"All modern computer science is derived from a single Veda"'::jsonb, '"The course includes arithmetic, geometry, trigonometry and algebra in ancient texts"'::jsonb, '"Classify the study as CSS animation"'::jsonb, '"Analyse the specified environmental practice and settlement/forest-management context with evidence"'::jsonb, '"Treat forests as a Vedanga"'::jsonb, '"Use only grammar definitions"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

