VALUES (4400991101010111, ARRAY['"A student has 14 study headings and must sort them into the conventional Caturdaśa-Vidyāsthāna scheme. Which composition should guide the first pass?"'::jsonb, '"A report compares an irrigation canal, a rainwater harvesting structure and a town plan. Which source-area grouping best supports the comparison?"'::jsonb, '"A student finds a claim that Sanskrit word structure may help computational language analysis. Which evaluation is most appropriate?"'::jsonb, '"A class compares Karma and rebirth with Moksha. Which relationship is the most appropriate high-level summary of the syllabus topics?"'::jsonb, '"A report combines ancient mathematics and astronomy but has only evidence about one calendar. How should the claim be narrowed?"'::jsonb, '"Which comparison best distinguishes Yajurveda and Samaveda in a basic Veda overview?"'::jsonb, '"A local-history project considers water management and trade connections. Which pair of topics fits the syllabus?"'::jsonb, '"A team describes a site as showing ''urban planning'' but gives only a photograph with no scale, date or site context. What is the main limitation?"'::jsonb, '"An ethical-living presentation needs to include duty, prosperity, enjoyment and liberation. What structure avoids omitting any Purushartha?"'::jsonb, '"A student''s notes define Jyotisha as poetic metre and Chandas as calendar study. Which correction is needed?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Four Vedas plus ten types of architecture only"'::jsonb, '"Four Vedas, six Vedangas, and four additional branches such as Mimamsa, Nyaya, Purana and Dharmashastra"'::jsonb, '"Four forms of HTML and ten CSS selectors"'::jsonb, '"Four Ashramas, four Purusharthas and six metals"'::jsonb, '"Only astronomy calendars"'::jsonb, '"Only language sciences"'::jsonb, '"Water management and architecture/planning within the technology unit"'::jsonb, '"Only the Purusharthas"'::jsonb, '"It proves every NLP system requires Sanskrit"'::jsonb, '"It is unrelated because computation never uses language structure"'::jsonb, '"It establishes a metalworking technique"'::jsonb, '"It aligns with the syllabus topic, but a specific computational performance claim still needs evidence"'::jsonb, '"Karma and rebirth concern action and continuing existence; Moksha concerns liberation"'::jsonb, '"Moksha is a measurement of weight"'::jsonb, '"Karma is a computer peripheral"'::jsonb, '"They are all names for poetic metre"'::jsonb, '"Classify the calendar as a Veda"'::jsonb, '"Claim every historical calendar followed it"'::jsonb, '"State what the examined calendar demonstrates and avoid claiming it represents every tradition or period"'::jsonb, '"Remove the evidence and assert universality"'::jsonb, '"Yajurveda is associated with ritual formulas; Samaveda with chants/melodies"'::jsonb, '"Yajurveda is metre; Samaveda is grammar"'::jsonb, '"Yajurveda is a Purana; Samaveda is a Vedanga"'::jsonb, '"Both are types of temple architecture"'::jsonb, '"Brahmacharya and Sannyasa"'::jsonb, '"Irrigation/water management and transportation/trading techniques"'::jsonb, '"Inline and external CSS"'::jsonb, '"Shiksha and Chandas"'::jsonb, '"A photograph alone gives all design rules"'::jsonb, '"The photo proves the site''s exact date"'::jsonb, '"Urban planning is not a syllabus topic"'::jsonb, '"The evidence is insufficient to support a detailed historical interpretation"'::jsonb, '"Dharma, Artha, Kama and Moksha"'::jsonb, '"Rigveda, Samaveda, Chandas and Kalpa"'::jsonb, '"Brahmacharya, Grihastha, Nyaya and Vastu"'::jsonb, '"Time, distance, weight and calendars"'::jsonb, '"Jyotisha is a Veda; Chandas is a Purana"'::jsonb, '"Both concern CSS positioning"'::jsonb, '"Jyotisha relates to astronomy/timekeeping; Chandas studies metre"'::jsonb, '"Jyotisha is grammar; Chandas is metalworking"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

