VALUES (4400991101010112, ARRAY['"A case study tries to show that a particular reservoir reflects historical water-management knowledge. What is the strongest evidence plan?"'::jsonb, '"A student wants to compare four Vedas, six Vedangas and four other branches without mixing categories. What is the correct count check?"'::jsonb, '"A presentation links traditional measurement with modern scientific units. Which method is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"A team is asked to discuss a temple''s form through the syllabus''s architecture themes. Which topics are most directly relevant?"'::jsonb, '"An argument claims Moksha is simply a synonym for material prosperity. What is the best correction?"'::jsonb, '"A researcher has evidence about textile dyeing from one site but wants to describe all ancient India. What wording is best?"'::jsonb, '"A student must describe the life-stage model but accidentally includes Dharma, Artha, Kama and Moksha. What is the correction?"'::jsonb, '"A project compares the role of calendars with agriculture-related star knowledge. What is the most relevant topic pair?"'::jsonb, '"A student wants to distinguish a supported syllabus fact from a historical hypothesis. Which practice is best?"'::jsonb, '"Which conclusion best reflects the full range of the BKS course described in the source?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Infer details solely from the general syllabus"'::jsonb, '"Use only the modern name of the reservoir"'::jsonb, '"Combine site-specific records or credible studies with analysis of storage, supply and setting"'::jsonb, '"Assume every reservoir belongs to the same tradition"'::jsonb, '"4+4+4=12"'::jsonb, '"6+6+4=16"'::jsonb, '"4×6=24"'::jsonb, '"4+6+4=14"'::jsonb, '"Define each unit, identify its historical/source context and state any conversion assumptions"'::jsonb, '"Ignore whether units measure time, distance or weight"'::jsonb, '"Use only a calendar illustration"'::jsonb, '"Treat every historical unit as exactly one modern unit without evidence"'::jsonb, '"Recycle Bin and shell commands"'::jsonb, '"Vastu Shastra, civil architecture and temple architecture"'::jsonb, '"NLP, HTML forms and email signatures"'::jsonb, '"HCF, LCM and polynomial identities"'::jsonb, '"Moksha is grammar and Artha is metre"'::jsonb, '"Both are Vedas"'::jsonb, '"Both are units of distance"'::jsonb, '"Moksha refers to liberation; Artha is the Purushartha associated with material means"'::jsonb, '"The site proves a universal rule"'::jsonb, '"This site provides an example of textile dyeing practice; broader prevalence needs additional evidence"'::jsonb, '"Textile dyeing is a Purushartha"'::jsonb, '"All places used precisely the same technique"'::jsonb, '"Ashramas name the four Vedas"'::jsonb, '"Those are all Vedangas"'::jsonb, '"Those are Purusharthas; Ashramas are Brahmacharya, Grihastha, Vanaprastha and Sannyasa"'::jsonb, '"The two lists are identical"'::jsonb, '"Vedanga Jyotish/time-calendar and Nakshatrara Gyaan/agriculture"'::jsonb, '"Vyakarana and textile dyeing"'::jsonb, '"Karma and CPU memory"'::jsonb, '"Purana and CSS shadows"'::jsonb, '"Remove all source notes"'::jsonb, '"Label the syllabus fact clearly and cite independent, case-specific evidence for the hypothesis"'::jsonb, '"Use confidence of wording as evidence"'::jsonb, '"Treat every hypothesis as verified because it fits the theme"'::jsonb, '"It is only a language grammar course"'::jsonb, '"It is limited to rituals and excludes scientific topics"'::jsonb, '"It is only a construction course"'::jsonb, '"It spans textual and philosophical traditions, science/mathematics and technology/architecture"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

