VALUES (4400912101010110, ARRAY['"A claimant argues that because a policy appears in Part IV, courts must enforce it as if it were a Fundamental Right. Which constitutional text most directly challenges that claim?"'::jsonb, '"A law makes an unequal classification. The government explains a legitimate aim, but the classification has no rational connection to that aim. Which issue remains?"'::jsonb, '"A person is denied personal liberty under an executive order with no lawful procedure. The authority says that administrative convenience is sufficient. Which response best reflects Article 21?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment is challenged as abolishing the essential democratic character of the Constitution. Which sequence of analysis is most appropriate for a course-level answer?"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble''s words ''Secular'' and ''Socialist'' were inserted by an amendment. Which statement about that history is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A Fundamental Duty to protect the environment is cited to automatically deny a person''s otherwise lawful speech. Which conclusion is most careful?"'::jsonb, '"A new state policy is consistent with a Directive Principle but is implemented in a way that violates Article 21. What follows?"'::jsonb, '"A state Governor and a Chief Minister disagree about the ordinary political direction of a state government. Which principle best describes their normal roles?"'::jsonb, '"A city and a rural district are designing local institutions. Which pairing is most consistent with the syllabus?"'::jsonb, '"A student says the ECI is responsible for every municipal poll because Article 324 covers elections. What is the best correction?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Article 51A(k)"'::jsonb, '"Article 37"'::jsonb, '"Article 21"'::jsonb, '"Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Whether it was published in a newspaper"'::jsonb, '"Whether the Governor attended a meeting"'::jsonb, '"Whether the classification meets Article 14''s equality/non-arbitrariness requirements"'::jsonb, '"Whether a municipal ward has been renumbered"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 applies only to corporations"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 concerns only the right to vote"'::jsonb, '"Convenience always overrides liberty"'::jsonb, '"Personal liberty cannot be deprived except according to procedure established by law"'::jsonb, '"Identify the alleged basic feature and assess it under the basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Treat every amendment as automatically invalid"'::jsonb, '"Check only whether the amendment title contains the word democratic"'::jsonb, '"Ask the municipal corporation to ratify the amendment"'::jsonb, '"They were included only by the 86th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"They were added to the original text in 1947"'::jsonb, '"They were added by the 42nd Amendment in 1976"'::jsonb, '"They are found only in Article 324"'::jsonb, '"The duty is relevant, but a restriction on speech must still be assessed under the constitutional provisions governing that freedom"'::jsonb, '"Environmental protection is not mentioned in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A applies only to municipal officers"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duties automatically override every right"'::jsonb, '"Only Parliament''s Speaker can evaluate it"'::jsonb, '"Its policy objective alone does not eliminate the need to comply with applicable Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"Part IV automatically overrides Part III"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 does not apply to government action"'::jsonb, '"The Governor is the elected day-to-day political leader"'::jsonb, '"The Chief Minister is appointed by the municipal corporation"'::jsonb, '"The District Collector is the constitutional head of the state"'::jsonb, '"The Governor is constitutional head while the Chief Minister leads the elected government and Council of Ministers"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation—urban local government; Zila Panchayat—district-level rural local government"'::jsonb, '"Both bodies are election courts"'::jsonb, '"Zila Panchayat—House of Parliament; Municipal Corporation—state Cabinet"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation—rural district; Zila Panchayat—Union legislature"'::jsonb, '"No constitutional body administers local elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 covers only school elections"'::jsonb, '"The Constitution separately provides State Election Commissions for Panchayat and municipal elections"'::jsonb, '"Municipal polls are run by Lok Sabha"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

