VALUES (4400912101010111, ARRAY['"A law classifies citizens by a criterion unrelated to its stated goal; affected people also claim the criterion burdens an Article 19 freedom. What is the strongest analytical approach?"'::jsonb, '"An administrator relies on an environmental duty to justify all restrictions on a public meeting. What should a balanced legal analysis do?"'::jsonb, '"A constitutional amendment changes the composition of a body, and challengers claim the change damages separation of powers and judicial review. What evidence is most important to the basic-structure question?"'::jsonb, '"A welfare scheme relies on a Directive Principle and denies a benefit through an arbitrary process. What is the most accurate conclusion?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen challenges an order affecting personal liberty. The authority claims Article 21 only applies when a law is completely absent, not when procedure exists but is arbitrary. Which response best reflects modern constitutional reasoning at course level?"'::jsonb, '"An interpretation dispute involves an ambiguous provision. One interpretation better advances justice, liberty and equality while remaining consistent with the text. How may the Preamble be used?"'::jsonb, '"The Union government loses Lok Sabha confidence but claims the Council of Ministers answers only to Rajya Sabha. Which constitutional feature refutes the claim?"'::jsonb, '"An election dispute concerns a Lok Sabha constituency, while a separate dispute concerns a municipal ward poll. Which institutional distinction is relevant at the outset?"'::jsonb, '"A person says all Directive Principles are individually enforceable in court because they are ''fundamental in governance''. Which reasoning corrects the conflation?"'::jsonb, '"A government claims equal protection demands the same outcome for every person regardless of materially relevant differences. What response is more accurate?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Assume a single Article automatically decides all claims"'::jsonb, '"Treat the matter only as a Fundamental Duty"'::jsonb, '"Assess equality/non-arbitrariness under Article 14 and separately test any Article 19 restriction against its applicable constitutional grounds"'::jsonb, '"Refer the policy to a Zila Panchayat for constitutional interpretation"'::jsonb, '"Treat Article 51A as the only enforceable right"'::jsonb, '"Assume public meetings are always prohibited"'::jsonb, '"Reject environmental protection as a constitutional concern"'::jsonb, '"Recognize Article 51A''s environmental duty but independently assess the restriction under the applicable rights and lawful procedure"'::jsonb, '"The amendment''s actual legal effects on the alleged foundational features, considered under the basic-structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Whether the amendment uses formal language"'::jsonb, '"Whether a state Governor publicly supports the amendment"'::jsonb, '"How many local wards exist"'::jsonb, '"Because welfare is a goal, all procedures are valid"'::jsonb, '"The scheme''s objective may be relevant, but its arbitrary implementation can still raise Article 14 concerns"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles are meaningless and must be ignored"'::jsonb, '"The denial can never be reviewed"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 only applies during elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 and 21 cannot ever be considered together"'::jsonb, '"Any written procedure automatically validates every deprivation"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 protection includes scrutiny of the legal procedure affecting life and liberty; the existence of a procedure alone does not end analysis"'::jsonb, '"As a local administration manual"'::jsonb, '"As an interpretive aid that illuminates constitutional objectives while the provision''s text remains controlling"'::jsonb, '"As an authority to disregard the operative text"'::jsonb, '"As a substitute for all judicial reasoning"'::jsonb, '"The President presides over Rajya Sabha daily"'::jsonb, '"State Governors supervise Union ministers"'::jsonb, '"Collective responsibility to Lok Sabha"'::jsonb, '"The State Election Commission''s municipal remit"'::jsonb, '"ECI administers the parliamentary election; State EC administers municipal elections under the local-body framework"'::jsonb, '"Both are conducted only by the Supreme Court"'::jsonb, '"The President organizes both directly"'::jsonb, '"Both are necessarily conducted by Municipal Corporation itself"'::jsonb, '"Only the President can decide enforceability"'::jsonb, '"Article 37 expressly distinguishes their governance importance from direct court enforceability"'::jsonb, '"Part IV is actually Part III"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A makes every policy court-enforceable"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 prohibits all different treatment"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only applies to local elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 overrides every other provision automatically"'::jsonb, '"Equal protection allows reasonable classification but not arbitrary discrimination"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

