VALUES (4400912101010112, ARRAY['"A law limits a citizen''s expression, uses a classification that may be arbitrary, and is defended as advancing a public-policy objective. Which review sequence is most defensible?"'::jsonb, '"A parent fails to provide educational opportunities to a child aged 8. Which pair most accurately separates a Fundamental Duty from the related right?"'::jsonb, '"A local administration proposal mixes city drainage services and district rural development. Which institutional design best reflects the course distinctions?"'::jsonb, '"A student must explain why constitutionalism matters when officials exercise emergency-like discretion. Which answer is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment is challenged as undermining a foundational feature, but the challenger merely says the new text is different. What must the argument add?"'::jsonb, '"A student states the Election Commission of India administers municipal elections because Article 324 concerns election control. Which constitutional arrangement resolves the point?"'::jsonb, '"A state policy seeks environmental improvement, but an official arbitrarily denies access to a public benefit. What is a balanced analysis?"'::jsonb, '"A person cites a Directive Principle as the sole basis to demand a directly enforceable order. Which qualification should be included?"'::jsonb, '"A constitutional issue concerns equal treatment, personal liberty and a policy directive. Which response is methodologically sound?"'::jsonb, '"A local government officer claims their administrative decisions are outside constitutional limits because the office is local, not national. Which principle best answers that claim?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Review only the Preamble, ignoring the Articles"'::jsonb, '"Apply Article 324 because every public dispute is electoral"'::jsonb, '"Accept the objective as conclusive and stop"'::jsonb, '"Examine the relevant Article 19 ground/reasonableness, assess the classification under Article 14, and consider the policy objective without treating it as a complete defence"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k) states the parental/guardian duty; Article 21A concerns the right to education for ages 6–14"'::jsonb, '"The 73rd Amendment creates both"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 is the duty and Article 19 is the right"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 is the duty and Article 51A is a right"'::jsonb, '"Give both tasks to the Rajya Sabha"'::jsonb, '"Use the Municipal Corporation for urban local-government functions and the Zila Panchayat for district-level rural local government, subject to applicable state arrangements"'::jsonb, '"Assign both to the Election Commission of India"'::jsonb, '"Treat both as functions of the Prime Minister personally"'::jsonb, '"It means there is no separation of functions"'::jsonb, '"It means only local bodies are bound by laws"'::jsonb, '"It means power is structured and limited by constitutional rules, rights and institutional checks"'::jsonb, '"It means officials may ignore law if their goal seems useful"'::jsonb, '"A reasoned connection between the amendment''s practical/legal effect and an alleged basic feature"'::jsonb, '"Only the date it was introduced"'::jsonb, '"The amendment''s page count"'::jsonb, '"The names of all members of the legislature"'::jsonb, '"Municipal elections are outside the Constitution entirely"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation appoints ECI members"'::jsonb, '"Part IXA provides a State Election Commission framework for municipality elections, while ECI handles elections assigned under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Lok Sabha runs municipal wards directly"'::jsonb, '"Assume Article 14 applies only during elections"'::jsonb, '"Assume Fundamental Duties erase all legal procedures"'::jsonb, '"Treat the environmental aim as an automatic exemption from equality"'::jsonb, '"Recognize the environmental aim and Article 51A duty, while also assessing whether the decision complies with applicable rights such as Article 14"'::jsonb, '"They are listed in Article 324"'::jsonb, '"They guide State policy and are important in governance, but Article 37 says they are not directly enforceable by courts"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles are superior to every constitutional right"'::jsonb, '"They apply only to local councils"'::jsonb, '"Apply only Article 51A to every dispute"'::jsonb, '"Assume Part IV repeals Part III"'::jsonb, '"Identify the separate questions under Article 14, Article 21 and Part IV, then interpret them together rather than treating one as automatic trump"'::jsonb, '"Refer it to a municipal corporation as the final constitutional court"'::jsonb, '"Public authorities at all levels must act within applicable constitutional and legal limits"'::jsonb, '"Constitutionalism applies only during general elections"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Rights apply only to Union ministers"'::jsonb, '"Only Parliament must follow law"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

